      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Turn 3. Opponent played Brightmare (2/3) which tapped my Silhana Wayfinder and gained 2 life (now at 22). They drew a card from Scroll of Avacyn too. I drew Elvish Rejuvenator.\n\
\n\
Let me think about my play:\n\
- I have Forest + Thriving Grove = 2 mana, and can play a land for 3.\n\
- **Dwynen's Elite** (1G): I control Silhana Wayfinder (an Elf), so this creates a 1/1 Elf token too! Great value.\n\
- **Elvish Rejuvenator** (2G): Ramps me, but costs 3 mana. I'd need to play Forest first.\n\
\n\
Play Forest, then I have 3 mana. Should I play Dwynen's Elite (2 mana, gets 2 bodies) or Elvish Rejuvenator (3 mana, ramps)?\n\
\n\
Dwynen's Elite gives me 2 bodies for 2 mana, leaving 1 mana for Elven Bow. If I play Elite + Elven Bow, I get a 2/2, a 1/1 token, and an equipment. That's a lot of board presence for 3 mana.\n\
\n\
Or: Elvish Rejuvenator to ramp into Wildheart Invoker next turn. But Invoker is a 4-drop, and I need the board presence more right now.\n\
\n\
I'll go with Forest → Dwynen's Elite → Elven Bow. Maximum board development.",
