    {
      "ts": "2026-03-09T18:22:11.853942-07:00",
      "seq": 73,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Now I have 4 mana and Wildheart Invoker is castable. Let me think:\n\
\n\
- **Wildheart Invoker** (2GG, 4/3): Big body, uses all 4 mana. The {8} ability is unlikely to be relevant.\n\
- **Elvish Rejuvenator** (2G, 1/1): Ramps but small body. Helps reach 8 mana for Invoker's ability? No, that's too slow.\n\
- **Ghirapur Guide** (2G, 3/2): Decent body, can make a creature unblockable for {2}{G}. Good with Elven Bow equipped.\n\
\n\
Wildheart Invoker is the biggest body at 4/3. It applies the most pressure. The opponent has two 2/3s. With a 4/3 Invoker, I can attack profitably — they can block with one creature but it trades favorably for me (4 power kills their 3 toughness, their 2 power doesn't kill my 3 toughness... wait, Invoker is 4/3 and their blockers are 2/3. If they block with one 2/3, my 4/3 kills it and survives with 1 toughness).\n\
\n\
Actually, let me consider Ghirapur Guide (3/2) + equip Elven Bow ({2}). That's 3+2 = 5 mana, and I only have 4. So I can't do both.\n\
\n\
Wildheart Invoker is the best play — biggest body on the board.",
