    {
      "ts": "2026-03-09T18:23:00.351516-07:00",
      "seq": 81,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Combat time! I can attack with Silhana Wayfinder (2/1), Dwynen's Elite (2/2), and Elf Warrior Token (1/1).\n\
\n\
Opponent has Brightmare (2/3) that can block and Celestial Enforcer (2/3) that's summoning sick — wait, summoning sickness doesn't prevent blocking! Both can block.\n\
\n\
Let me think about attacks:\n\
- If I attack with all 3 (2/1, 2/2, 1/1 = 5 total power), opponent has 2 blockers.\n\
- They block Dwynen's Elite 2/2 with Brightmare 2/3 → Elite dies, Brightmare lives at 2/1 damage. Bad trade.\n\
- They block Wayfinder 2/1 with Brightmare 2/3 → Wayfinder dies, Brightmare lives. Bad.\n\
- If they block with both, they can stop 2 attackers. 1 gets through.\n\
\n\
Actually, I should attack with all 3. If they double-block, they stop 2 but 1 gets through. If they single-block, 2 get through. Either way I'm dealing damage and applying pressure. The worst case is they block the 2/2 and the 2/1 with their 2/3s, but Enforcer has summoning sickness... no wait, that doesn't matter for blocking.\n\
\n\
Let me reconsider: They have 2 blockers (both 2/3). If I attack with all 3:\n\
- They can block 2 of my 3 attackers\n\
- Brightmare blocks Dwynen's Elite: 2/3 vs 2/2 → Elite dies, Brightmare takes 2 (survives at 2/1)\n\
- Enforcer blocks Wayfinder: 2/3 vs 2/1 → Wayfinder dies, Enforcer takes 2 (survives at 2/1)\n\
- Elf token gets through for 1\n\
\n\
I'd lose 2 creatures, they lose 0, and I deal 1 damage. That's terrible.\n\
\n\
Better to just attack with all 3 and hope they don't block optimally, or not attack at all and wait for next turn when Invoker can attack too.\n\
\n\
Actually, attacking with everything is bad because I lose bodies. Let me think about what to hold back.\n\
\n\
If I attack with just the Elf Warrior Token (1/1), they can block it with either creature. Not useful.\n\
\n\
If I attack with Dwynen's Elite (2/2) and Elf Token (1/1), they block one with Brightmare. If they block Elite, token gets through for 1 and Elite dies. If they block token, Elite gets through for 2 and token dies. Either way I lose a creature.\n\
\n\
The key question: is dealing 1-2 damage worth losing a creature? Not really at this stage. I should hold back and attack next turn with Invoker leading the charge.\n\
\n\
Wait, but they also have Celestial Enforcer — if they get a flyer, they can start tapping my creatures. I need to be aggressive before they set up.\n\
\n\
Actually, I think the best play is to send in the Elf Warrior Token alone. If they block a 1/1 token, that's fine — they wasted a block on a token. If they don't block, I deal 1. The token is my least valuable creature.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but they will just block the token if I send it alone. Let me just skip attacks and present the full squad next turn with Invoker.",
