    {
      "ts": "2026-03-09T18:24:35.639351-07:00",
      "seq": 92,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Good, Ivy Lane Denizen resolved. No more mana available. Time for combat!\n\
\n\
My attackable creatures: Dwynen's Elite 2/2, Elf Warrior Token 1/1, Silhana Wayfinder 2/1, Wildheart Invoker 4/3. That's 9 power total.\n\
\n\
Opponent's blockers: Brightmare 2/3, Celestial Enforcer 2/3, Anointed Chorister 1/1 (sick, but can still block).\n\
\n\
If I attack with everything:\n\
- 9 power attacking vs 3 potential blockers\n\
- They can block 3 of my 4 attackers\n\
- Best for them: Block Invoker 4/3 with Brightmare + Enforcer (double block kills it, both survive), block something else with Chorister\n\
- Actually Brightmare (2/3) alone doesn't kill Invoker (4/3): deals 2, Invoker survives. Invoker deals 4 to Brightmare, killing it.\n\
\n\
So optimal blocks for opponent:\n\
- Block Invoker with Brightmare: Brightmare dies, Invoker takes 2 (survives at 4/1)\n\
- Block Dwynen's Elite with Enforcer: Elite takes 2 (dies), Enforcer takes 2 (survives at 2/1)\n\
- Block Elf Token with Chorister: Token dies, Chorister takes 1 (survives)\n\
- Wayfinder gets through for 2\n\
\n\
Result: I lose Elite and Token, they lose Brightmare. I deal 2 damage. Not great.\n\
\n\
Better: Attack with just Invoker and Wayfinder:\n\
- If they block Invoker with Brightmare: Brightmare dies, Invoker survives. Wayfinder deals 2. I deal 2, they lose Brightmare.\n\
- If they double block Invoker: It might die. 2+2 = 4 damage to a 4/3, it dies. They keep both blockers. Wayfinder gets through for 2.\n\
\n\
Actually, attacking with everyone forces them to make hard choices. Let me attack with all 4. The key insight: they probably don't want to trade Brightmare into Invoker because Invoker kills it. Their best play might be to chump with Chorister and let some damage through.\n\
\n\
Let me attack with all 4 creatures. They have to choose wisely.",
