      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Opponent attacking with Brightmare (2/3) and Celestial Enforcer (2/3) for 4 damage. I have Reclamation Sage (2/1) to block. Elf Token is tapped from attacking.\n\
\n\
If I block:\n\
- Block Brightmare: Sage deals 2 to Brightmare (survives at 2/1), Brightmare deals 2 to Sage (dies since 2>1). I take 2 from Enforcer. Net: lose Sage, take 2.\n\
- Block Enforcer: Same math. Sage dies, Enforcer survives. I take 2 from Brightmare.\n\
- Don't block: I take 4.\n\
\n\
I should block to save 2 life. Sage is a 2/1 that's already done its job (destroyed Light of Promise). Trading it for 2 damage prevention is fine. I'll block Celestial Enforcer since its tap ability is more threatening long-term (even though Sage dies either way).\n\
\n\
Wait - actually Sage dies either way and neither of their creatures die. So blocking doesn't trade, it just prevents 2 damage. Still worth it. Let me block whichever I want to prevent damage from. I'll block Enforcer.",
