\n\
If I attack with 4 creatures:\n\
1 Flyer (unblocked) -> 3 dmg.\n\
3 Ground vs 2 Blockers.\n\
At least 1 ground gets through -> 1 or 2 dmg.\n\
Total ~4-5 dmg. Opponent goes to 7-8.\n\
\n\
If they block `Brightmare` with `Rec Sage`, they trade 2/1 for 2/3. Good for them? 2/3 is valuable.\n\
But I have `Feat of Resistance` up! `{1}{W}`.\n\
I have 4 lands.\n\
If I attack, I can hold up `Feat`.\n\
If they block, I can give protection from Green.\n\
`Brightmare` (2/3) blocked by `Rec Sage` (2/1 Green).\n\
I cast Feat (1W). Brightmare gains Prot Green and +1/+1 counter.\n\
It becomes 3/4, takes 0 dmg, kills Rec Sage.\n\
This is a blowout.\n\
\n\
Plan:\n\
Attack with ALL.\n\
Hold up `Feat of Resistance`.\n\
If they block favorably for me (e.g. chump), fine.\n\
If they block to trade (Rec Sage on Brightmare or Enforcer), I blow them out with Feat.\n\
