But attacking with a 2/3 is usually better than tapping a specific blocker if I'm planning to alpha strike soon.\n\
Actually, tapping a blocker removes it from combat entirely correctly?\n\
If I use Enforcer to tap `Reclamation Sage`:\n\
I attack with Angel (3/3), Brightmare (2/3), Chorister (1/1).\n\
Blockers: `Elvish Rejuvenator` (1/1).\n\
It blocks Brightmare. 1 dmg to Brightmare. Rejuvenator dies.\n\
Angel hits (3). Chorister hits (1). Total 4 dmg.\n\
Board clear of blockers except token next turn.\n\
BUT, Enforcer costs 2 mana to activate. I have 4 total. So I'd have 2 left.\n\
I can still hold up `Feat`.\n\
\n\
Option A: Attack with all 4. 4 untapped mana. Feat available.\n\
Option B: Tap Rec Sage with Enforcer. Attack with 3. 2 untapped mana. Feat available.\n\
\n\
Option A is more aggressive.\n\
If they block Rec Sage on Enforcer -> I Feat Enforcer. It lives, Rec Sage dies.\n\
If they block Rec Sage on Brightmare -> I Feat Brightmare. It lives.\n\
If they block Rec Sage on Angel (if they had reach) -> ...\n\
The only way they punish Option A is if they have TWO blockers that can double block something effectively, or a combat trick.\n\
