      "reasoning": "**Post-Combat Strategy**\n\
\n\
The attack was a HUGE success!\n\
Opponent took 8 damage (from 12 down to 4).\n\
They didn't block at all.\n\
I gained 1 life (Brightmare lifelink?), I am at 26.\n\
Wait, `Brightmare` has lifelink? \"2/3 Lifelink\" (Let's assume, or I gained life from something else).\n\
My life total is 26. Opponent is 4.\n\
\n\
I have 4 untapped Plains.\n\
Hand: `Anointed Chorister` (1), `Feat of Resistance` (2), `Voice of the Provinces` (6).\n\
I can cast `Anointed Chorister` for {W} (1 mana).\n\
This leaves 3 mana open.\n\
`Feat of Resistance` costs {1}{W} (2 mana).\n\
So I can cast Chorister and still hold up Feat.\n\
Current board: All my creatures are tapped.\n\
Opponent has: `Elf Warrior Token` (tapped), `Reclamation Sage` (2/1, untapped), `Elvish Rejuvenator` (1/1, untapped).\n\
Wait, Rejuvenator was sick last turn. Now it's not. It didn't block.\n\
If I cast Chorister (1/1), it will be a blocker.\n\
Opponent has 4 power ready to attack (2+1 = 3? No, token is tapped).\n\
Actually, Rejuvenator is untapped?\n\
If Rec Sage + Rejuvenator attack = 3 damage.\n\
I am at 26. I don't care.\n\
\n\
Playing Chorister adds to my board presence for lethal next turn.\n\
It's just a 1/1, but it widens my board.\n\
If opponent has a sweeper (unlikely in green/white/elf deck), I lose it.\n\
But if I don't play it, I don't utilize my mana efficiently? I have plenty of mana next turn (5 lands drop?).\n\
Wait, I haven't played a land this turn. I don't have a land in hand.\n\
I have 4 lands.\n\
Next turn I draw. If I draw a land -> `Voice of the Provinces` (6 mana). Need 6th land.\n\
So 5th land next turn doesn't cast Voice.\n\
So playing Chorister is fine.\n\
Also, if I play Chorister, I have a blocker for his 2/1 or 1/1 stuff.\n\
It preserves my life total slightly.\n\
More importantly, it forces him to deal with another body.\n\
With him at 4 life, any creature is a threat.\n\
`Anointed Chorister` can be pumped later.\n\
\n\
I'll cast `Anointed Chorister`.\n\
Hold up `Feat`.\n\
\n\
Also, notice `Elvish Rejuvenator` is labeled `(sick)` in the last prompt?\n\
Ah, \"Elvish Rejuvenator 1/1 (sick)\".\n\
Wait, opponent cast it on THEIR turn (Turn 7 PRECOMBAT_MAIN).\n\
It should not be sick on MY turn (Turn 8).\n\
Why does it say sick?\n\
Maybe buggy display? Or maybe I miscounted turns?\n\
If it's sick, it can't block? It didn't block.\n\
Regardless, I'm happy.\n\
\n\
Sidenote: I should check if I have a land drop.\n\
\"Land drops remaining: 1\".\n\
Hand: `Anointed Chorister`, `Feat`, `Voice`.\n\
No lands in hand.\n\
So I play Chorister.\n\
\n\
Action: Cast `Anointed Chorister` [id=p70].\n\
Then pass turn holding `Feat`.\n\
\n\
Chat: \"That went well.\"\n\
Actually, \"You're on the ropes!\"\n\
Let's just play.\n\
\n\
Wait, opponent didn't block ANYTHING.\n\
This means they probably have a plan for their turn?\n\
Overrun? (Standard limited finisher).\n\
But they are at 4 life.\n\
If they don't have a sweeper or mass lifegain, they are dead to my flyer alone next turn.\n\
So I just need to survive.\n\
Blocking with a new Chorister helps survive.\n\
\n\
Cast Chorister.\n\
\n\
Also, `Feat of Resistance` can protect my creatures from removal on his turn.\n\
Say he tries to `Rabid Bite` my Angel. I Feat in response.\n\
So holding 2 mana is critical.\n\
Casting Chorister leaves 3 mana.\n\
Perfect.\n\
\n\
One detail: `Anointed Chorister` has an activated ability: `{4}{W}: +3/+3 and Flying`.\n\
If I draw a land, I'll have 5 mana next turn.\n\
If I have 5 mana, I can pump one Chorister to 4/4 Flying.\n\
That is lethal on its own if Angel is dealt with.\n\
Good redundancy.\n\
\n\
Proceed.",
