      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Elderleaf Mentor resolved with the token! Now I have 5 creatures: Elderleaf Mentor (3/2), Elf Warrior Token (1/1), Elf Warrior Token #2 (1/1), Elvish Rejuvenator (1/1), Reclamation Sage (2/1).\n\
\n\
I have 1 untapped Forest and 1 land drop. Can't cast anything else useful. Let me move to combat. Only non-sick creatures can attack: Elf Warrior Token #1, Rejuvenator, Reclamation Sage. Their creatures are all tapped! Free damage!\n\
\n\
But wait - I need these creatures to block next turn. If I attack with them and they're tapped, I can't block with them on their turn. With only sick creatures left to block (Mentor and Token #2), I can only block 2 of their 5 attackers. That would mean 5+ damage gets through, killing me.\n\
\n\
I should NOT attack this turn to keep all blockers available. The chip damage isn't worth dying for.",
